A narrative is your field journal for observations, field decisions, habitat
impressions, and context that do not fit into a specimen or event record.

## Creating a narrative

{% steps %}

1. Open the `Narrative` page {% ref id="A" /%} from the navigation bar.
2. Select the add icon {% ref id="B" /%} at the top right (or `Create
   narrative` from the empty screen or three-dot menu).
3. Enter `Date` {% ref id="C" /%} and, optionally, `Time`. Future dates cannot
   be chosen.
4. Select `Site ID` {% ref id="D" /%}. NAHPU shows the site's locality name
   below the field.

    {% aside type="note" %}

    Create at least one site on the [Sites page](/en/usages/sites) before
    linking a narrative to a site.

    {% /aside %}

5. Choose `Writer` {% ref id="E" /%} from the personnel assigned to the project.
6. Write your entry in the `Narrative` text area {% ref id="F" /%}.

{% /steps %}

All changes save automatically—there is no Save button. `Date` and `Time` are
stored separately:

- Entering a `Time` when `Date` is blank automatically sets `Date` to today.
- Clearing `Date` also clears `Time`; clearing `Time` keeps `Date`.

## Writing and previewing text

Narrative entries support Markdown. Select the eye/pencil toggle button
(`Preview` / `Edit`) {% ref id="I" /%} above the text field to switch between
writing and rendered views.

### Markdown cheat sheet

Plain text works fine—use the formatting below whenever longer notes benefit
from structure:

| What you want | What you type | What you get |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bold | `**set before dusk**` | **set before dusk** |
| Italic | `_Bunomys penitus_` | _Bunomys penitus_ |
| Strikethrough | `~~12 traps~~` | ~~12 traps~~ |
| Heading | `## Morning check` | a section heading |
| Bullet list | `- checked line 1` | a bulleted item |
| Numbered list | `1. checked line 1` | a numbered item |
| Checklist | `- [ ] rebait traps` | a checkbox item |
| Quote | `> guide reported rain` | an indented quote block |
| Code or fixed-width value | `` `GPHH-L1` `` | `GPHH-L1` |
| Link | `[GBIF](https://gbif.org)` | [GBIF](https://gbif.org) |

Three quick rules cover most of the rest:

- Leave a blank line between paragraphs (a single line break is treated as a
  space).
- Indent by four spaces to nest a list item under another item.
- Put `---` on its own line for a horizontal rule between sections.

Switch to `Preview` to verify formatting before moving on. NAHPU stores the raw
Markdown text, so exports and backups preserve what you typed.

## Adding media

Attach photos, videos, audio recordings, or files to a narrative using the
camera, audio recorder, device gallery, or file picker. Narrative media moves
with project transfers and can be included in exports when narrative media is
selected.

## Searching and managing narratives

Use the search button {% ref id="G" /%} in the app bar to filter entries, and
use the bottom page controls {% ref id="H" /%} to move between them. The
three-dot menu provides:

| Action | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `Create narrative` | Adds a new narrative entry. |
| `Sort records` | Chooses the sort field and direction for the list. |
| `Delete record` | Permanently deletes the current narrative and its media. |
| `Delete all records` | Permanently deletes every narrative in the active project. |

Deletion cannot be undone. Export or back up the project first if you may need
the entries later.
